body.en:
There is more than one way to solve a quadratic equation — factorisation, the quadratic formula, completing the square, or cancelling when both sides share the same factor. This lesson focuses on the three most useful:
(1) factorisation (find the roots with the calculator, then work back to the factors) — no need to force the cross-method;
(2) a factor on both sides: take it $=0$ first for one root, then cancel it for the other root;
(3) the quadratic formula $x=\frac{-b\pm\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a}$ — for surd roots or awkward coefficients.
Method 1 (calculator factorisation): on a Casio fx-50FH II press [FMLA 01] (or run Prog 1 on a fx-3650P II) and enter $a$, $b$, $c$ to get the two roots. Reverse rule: a fraction root $x=\frac{p}{q}$ gives the factor $(qx-p)$; an integer root $x=k$ gives $(x-k)$:
{{math:0}}
Method 2 (a factor on both sides): split it into two cases and no root is lost —
(a) first assume that common factor $=0$: it always satisfies the equation (both sides become 0), so you get one root straight away;
(b) for everything else (the factor is $\ne 0$), you may cancel it and solve the remaining linear equation — that gives the other root.
✗ Wrong (cancelling $x$ without splitting the cases): {{math:1}} → only $x=-8$ is left, $x=0$ is lost
✓ Right (split the cases first): {{math:2}}
This lesson's $(x-2t)(x-3t)=(6t-x)(x-3t)$ is exactly that kind: take $(x-3t)=0$ to get $x=3t$; in the other case cancel $(x-3t)$ to get $2x-8t=0$, i.e. $x=4t$ — both roots kept.
(“Move everything to one side and factor” is the advanced route — harder for students, so learn the two-case method above first.)
Method 3 (quadratic formula): use it when factorisation is not clean (surd roots): {{math:3}}
Finally: whichever method you use, always write every root (both sides of “or”).

body.zh:
卷二最愛考這種題：已知一個根，要求另一條式子的值 —— 做法通常是兩步：① 寫下 $a\alpha^{2}+b\alpha+c=0$；② 把方程整理成「$\alpha^{2}=$（一條含有 $\alpha$ 的式子）」，再整塊代入目標式：那個式子是分數也可以 —— 分子整塊乘，約簡時每一項都要除。
例：已知 $\alpha$ 是方程 $x^{2}-4x-2=0$ 的一個根，求 $3+8\alpha-2\alpha^{2}$ 的值。{{math:0}}
不需要求出 $\alpha$ 的數值（它通常是無理數）；用「根」這個關係就夠。
另一個例子：已知 $\beta$ 是方程 $3\beta^{2}-5\beta-7=0$ 的一個根，求 $4+10\beta-6\beta^{2}$ 的值。{{math:1}}

body.en:
A Paper 2 favourite: given one root, find the value of another expression — usually two steps: (1) write down $a\alpha^{2}+b\alpha+c=0$; (2) rearrange the equation into $\alpha^{2}=$ (an expression in $\alpha$), then substitute that whole expression into the target; a fraction is fine — multiply the whole numerator, and divide every term when cancelling.
Example: given that $\alpha$ is a root of $x^{2}-4x-2=0$, find the value of $3+8\alpha-2\alpha^{2}$. {{math:0}}
You do not need the value of $\alpha$ itself (it is usually irrational); the root relation is enough.
Another example: given that $\beta$ is a root of $3\beta^{2}-5\beta-7=0$, find the value of $4+10\beta-6\beta^{2}$. {{math:1}}

